---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Layers, ArrowLeft, Code2, Sparkles } from '@lucide/astro';

const title = "Mapping tables to entities";
const description = "Table-to-entity and DTO mapping in Litebridge";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="pt-32 pb-20 lg:pt-48 lg:pb-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mb-12 reveal">
        <a
          href="/examples"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-500 hover:text-accent dark:text-gray-400 dark:hover:text-accent transition-colors mb-6"
        >
          <ArrowLeft class="h-4 w-4" />
          Back to Examples
        </a>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-primary dark:text-white sm:text-6xl mb-6">
          Mapping tables to entities
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          Learn how Litebridge maps relational database tables to Java records, plain DTOs, and annotated entity classes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-12">
        <!-- Overview -->
        <section class="reveal">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-primary/10 text-primary dark:bg-accent/10 dark:text-accent">
              <Layers class="h-6 w-6" />
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary dark:text-white">Mapping Strategies</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            Litebridge provides flexible persistence modeling without requiring domain classes to inherit from framework-specific base classes. There are two primary approaches to entity registration:
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-dark-bg/60">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary/10 text-primary dark:bg-accent/10 dark:text-accent">
                  <Sparkles class="h-5 w-5" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-primary dark:text-white">Annotated Entities</h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Decorate domain classes using Litebridge annotations like <code class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-primary dark:text-accent">@Table</code> and <code class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-primary dark:text-accent">@Column</code>. Entities can be registered individually or scanned automatically from packages.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-dark-bg/60">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary/10 text-primary dark:bg-accent/10 dark:text-accent">
                  <Code2 class="h-5 w-5" />
                </div>
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-primary dark:text-white">Programmatic DTOs</h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Map plain unannotated DTOs and Java records via Litebridge's fluent registration API, separating database schema details completely from domain models.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Coming soon note -->
        <section class="reveal" style="transition-delay: 100ms">
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-gray-50 dark:bg-dark-bg/40 p-6 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-center sm:text-left">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
              Detailed examples for one-to-one, one-to-many relationships, custom converters, and composite primary keys will be covered in upcoming guides.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .reveal {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(20px);
    transition: all 0.8s ease-out;
  }

  .reveal.active {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
</style>
